      "role": "user",
      "content": "The Hapsburg and Lombard references are fascinating—it adds a real sense of historical weight and \"old-world\" gravity to the brief. It feels much more substantial than just a generic luxury look.\n\nI'm curious about the \"genetic archetype\" part of your strategy. Since we're essentially building an AI-driven model for the most elite echelon of society, how do we handle the potential for \"genetic drift\" or modern mixing in the casting? \n\nEssentially, if the casting engine encounters phenotypes that are clearly \"high-status\" in a modern, cosmopolitan sense but fall outside these specific historical European lineages, how should the brief instruct the AI to categorize them? Should we refine the brief to explicitly prioritize these classical European \"pure\" archetypes to maintain the campaign's exclusivity, or is there a way to reconcile modern global success with this specific historical baseline of prestige?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
